{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Agent enrollment: from an Enrollment Code to a tailnet node",
  "description": "How an Owner's Agent joins the tailnet: the web UI issues a single-use code, the Agent's command line exchanges it for a pre-auth key, and the control plane connects to the node once it joins.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/agents.go",
      "line": 50,
      "title": "The Owner asks for a code",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) issueCode`. The code is random, shown once, and only its hash is stored, valid for 15 minutes."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/agents.go",
      "line": 70,
      "title": "The Agent exchanges the code",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) enroll`. The code is used up, a single-use pre-auth key is made for the Owner's tag, and the Agent is recorded."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/store.go",
      "line": 95,
      "title": "Consuming a code once",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) useCode`. A code is marked used in one statement, so two enrollments cannot both win."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/headscale/client.go",
      "line": 70,
      "title": "The Tailnet port",
      "description": "`type Tailnet interface`. Headscale is called directly by the fleet service. Test: tailnettest.Fake."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/headscale/client.go",
      "line": 96,
      "title": "The real Tailnet client",
      "description": "`func New(config Config) *Client`. It talks to the Headscale REST API and installs the policy that keeps the tailnet default-deny."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/link.go",
      "line": 50,
      "title": "The control plane connects",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) reconcile(`. Every enrolled Agent whose node is on the tailnet gets a connection, and removed Agents lose theirs."
    }
  ]
}
